.TH SCOPEBRIDGE-TERM 1 "September 2026" "scopebridge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scopebridge-term \- a Rigol DS1000Z-E oscilloscope from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scopebridge-term
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.RI [ < " commands" ]
.br
.B scopebridge-term \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scopebridge-term
reads commands, one per line, from the keyboard or a pipe, and sends them
to
.BR scopebridge-server (1)
on
.IR HOST : N
(default 127.0.0.1:5026).
Numbers take SI suffixes: 500m, 2u, 1k.
Lines starting with # are comments. Read from a pipe, commands are echoed,
an error does not stop the rest, and the exit status is 1 if any command
failed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
The scope's settings.
.TP
.BR run " | " stop " | " single " | " auto " | " force
Acquisition.
.TP
.BI "ch " N " \fR[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR] [\fBscale \fIV\fR] [\fBoffset \fIV\fR] [\fBcoupling dc\fR|\fBac\fR|\fBgnd\fR] [\fBprobe \fIX\fR]"
A channel's settings.
.TP
.BI "tb \fR[\fBscale \fIS\fR] [\fBoffset \fIS\fR] [\fBmode yt\fR|\fBxy\fR|\fBroll\fR]"
The timebase.
.TP
.BI "acq \fR[\fBtype normal\fR|\fBaverage\fR|\fBpeak\fR|\fBhires\fR] [\fBaverages \fIN\fR] [\fBdepth auto\fR|\fIN\fR]"
The acquisition mode and memory depth; alone, shows them.
.TP
.BI "trig \fR[\fBlevel \fIV\fR] [\fBslope \fIS\fR] [\fBsource \fIS\fR] [\fBsweep \fIS\fR] [\fBmode \fIM\fR]"
The trigger.
.TP
.BI "measure " N " \fR[\fIITEM\fR ...]"
Measurements: freq period vpp vmax vmin vtop vbase vamp vavg vrms rise
fall pwidth nwidth pduty nduty.
.TP
.BI "watch \fR[\fIN\fR|\fBall\fR] [\fIFRAMES\fR]"
The live waveform, drawn with characters; Enter stops.
.TP
.BI "sleep " SECONDS
Pause.
.TP
.BI "wait \fR[\fISECONDS\fR]"
After
.BR single :
until the scope has triggered.
.TP
.BI "capture " N
Read channel N's whole acquisition memory into the server.
.TP
.BI "save " FILE " \fR[\fIN\fR]"
The captured samples as CSV.
.TP
.BI "spectrum " N " \fR[\fIWINDOW\fR]"
The strongest lines of the capture's spectrum.
.TP
.BI "decode uart\fR|\fBi2c\fR|\fBspi \fR[\fINAME VALUE\fR ...] [\fBshow \fIN\fR]"
Decode the captures as a serial bus; UART also prints the text per line.
UART:
.BR "tx " N ,
.BR "rx " N ,
.BR "baud " B ,
.BR "bits " N ,
.BR "parity none" | even | odd ,
.BR "stop 1" | 1.5 | 2 .
I2C:
.BR "scl " N ,
.BR "sda " N .
SPI:
.BR "clk " N ,
.BR "data " N ,
.BR "edge rising" | falling ,
.BR "width " N ,
.BR "timeout " S .
All:
.BR "inverted on" | off ,
.BR "msb_first on" | off ,
.BR "threshold1 " V ,
.BR "threshold2 " V .
.TP
.BI "bus \fR[\fB1\fR|\fB2\fR] \fBuart\fR|\fBi2c\fR|\fBspi \fR[\fINAME VALUE\fR ...] [\fBformat hex\fR|\fBascii\fR|\fBdec\fR|\fBbin\fR]"
Set up the scope's own bus decoder with the same settings;
.B "bus \fR[\fIB\fR] \fBoff"
switches it off.
.TP
.BI "timing " N " \fR[\fBto \fIM\fR] [\fBgap \fIS\fR] [\fBlow\fR] [\fBbins \fIN\fR] [\fBthreshold \fIV\fR]"
Time code: the blocks a program marks on channel
.I N
(high while they run, or low with
.BR low ).
Capture the channel first, and channel
.I M
too for
.BR to .
Shows the count, min, mean, max and standard deviation of the blocks,
the time between them and their period, where the longest and shortest
are, and a histogram; with
.BR to ,
the latency from each block to the next pulse on channel
.IR M ;
with
.BR gap ,
bursts of pulses split by pauses longer than
.I S
(one per run of a loop that toggles the pin).
.TP
.B mask
The pass/fail test's counts.
.TP
.BI "mask on\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBcreate\fR|\fBrun\fR|\fBstop\fR|\fBreset \fR[\fBx \fIDIV\fR] [\fBy \fIDIV\fR] [\fBsource ch1\fR|\fBch2\fR] [\fBstop_on_fail on\fR|\fBoff\fR] [\fBbeep on\fR|\fBoff\fR]"
Set up and run the pass/fail test.
.TP
.B ref
The reference waveforms the server keeps.
.TP
.BI "ref save " SLOT " " N " \fR| \fBref clear \fR[\fISLOT\fR] | \fBref export \fISLOT FILE"
Keep channel N's screen as a reference; forget one or all; write one as
CSV.
.TP
.BI "ref load " SLOT " " FILE " \fR[\fIN\fR]"
A CSV of time, volts as a reference, placed like channel N.
.TP
.BI "screenshot " FILE
The scope's screen as BMP.
.TP
.BI "setup save " FILE " \fR| \fBsetup load " FILE
The scope's complete setup.
.TP
.BI "scpi " TEXT
A raw SCPI command; a query (ending in ?) is answered.
.TP
.BI "raw " JSON
A protocol request as it is.
.TP
.B quit
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.RS
$ scopebridge-term <<END
ch 1 scale 500m offset \-1.5
tb scale 1m
single
wait
capture 1
spectrum 1 flattop
save capture.csv
END
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.scopebridgerc
The server's address, when
.B \-\-host
and
.B \-\-port
are not given:
.B host
and
.B port
in its
.B [client]
section.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scopebridge-server (1),
.BR scopebridge-gui (1),
.BR scopebridge-run (1)
